--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`. That path is
NOT a project.yml source group in this repo. The real, COMPILED canonical admin-page home is
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` — where the live sibling P7 admin pages ship (TeslaOrders,
ApiPlayground, DiskForecast, FleetTelemetryCoverage, SchemaDrift, RedisSignalViewer; the apple
ledger shows them "done"), and which project.yml lists as a `Sources` source path. swiftlint's
`included:` paths likewise cover `Sources`, not `TeslaSync/Features`. The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Admin`.
This is the SAME reconciliation the TeslaOrders / SchemaDrift / DiskForecast sibling logs recorded.
Strings ship in the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file).

STRING REUSE (covenant #2 — no scope narrowing, but no needless duplication / DRY): the two parity
strings already exist in the catalog from the web i18n extraction, with the EXACT web values and the
web key suffix:
    translation.region.title    = "Region & API"
    translation.region.subtitle = "Tesla account region and Fleet API endpoint"
The page binds those verbatim (web `useTranslation('settings')` `t('region.title' | 'region.subtitle')`).
The ONLY new catalog key added is `route.teslaRegion` ("Region & API") for the sidebar route title.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the TOP-LEVEL `/tesla-region` in the Account side-nav group
(Apple Layout.Nav "Account" group already lists nav("/tesla-region", "Region & API", "globe")).
A dedicated `.teslaRegion` AppRoute case is added (pathSegment "tesla-region", systemImage "globe"
= web globe, group .account). No AppRouteParser alias is needed — `/tesla-region` matches the
pathSegment on the first segment directly (verified by the executed test harness below).
TeslaRegionRouteRegistration hosts the page on that route; it is composed into `routeHostRegistry`
in TeslaSyncApp.swift, so the page is reachable via the Account-group sidebar entry and any
`/tesla-region` deep link.

@Observable BINDING (covenant #2): the web page holds NO state of its own (the manifest: "no API
data sources — renders from navigation values / local state"). Faithfully, the native page is pure
chrome that binds the embedded section's @Observable `RegionSettingsModel` (the P1/S8 state holder) —
NOT an empty stub page-model. The page takes the model and hands it to RegionSettings(model:),
mirroring the sibling TeslaOrdersPage(model:) shape. The embedded RegionSettings owns the 3 data
states (loading / empty / error) + data + stale/offline freshness — every state renders, no blank box.

